coder › Changed `overlaps` in `src/range.ts` and added tests in `src/range.test.ts`, on branch `fix/overlaps` (commits `24b08e1`, `47a1b55`).

What changed:
- `src/range.ts`: added a `toMs` helper that `Date.parse`s and throws `TypeError('Invalid date: <value>')` on `NaN`, so the offending value is in the message. `overlaps` now validates both ranges first, throwing `RangeError` when `end < start`, returns `false` when either range is zero-length (`start === end` in ms), and uses strict comparison `aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd` so touching ranges (one end exactly equals the other's start) do not overlap while same-start ranges do.
- `src/range.test.ts`: kept the existing shared-hour test and added tests for touching both ways (false), same start (true), zero-length vs normal / normal vs zero-length / itself (all false), unparsable start and unparsable end (each `TypeError` containing the bad value), and backwards range in either argument (`RangeError`).

